# (date, display name, born, died, patron of, life). Shown on Saint of the Day; Mass readings are not changed.
EXTRA = [
('01-20', 'Blessed Cyprian Michael Iwene Tansi', '1903, Aguleri, Nigeria', '20 January 1964, Leicester, England', ['priests'],
 'Iwene Tansi was born to a traditional family in Aguleri, in today\'s Anambra State, and was baptised Michael as a boy. After working as a teacher he was ordained a priest for the Archdiocese of Onitsha in 1937, one of the first Nigerian priests. For thirteen years he served tirelessly in parishes, known for his prayer, his care for families and his strict but loving guidance.\n\nIn 1950 he became a Trappist monk at Mount Saint Bernard Abbey in England, taking the name Cyprian, hoping one day to bring monastic life to Africa. He died there in 1964. Pope John Paul II beatified him in Onitsha in 1998, the first Nigerian to be beatified.'),
]
